ever since harry houdini's 1919 movie  the master mystery  robot stories have run the entire  spectrum of human emotion  we should know that for the purpose of  this list robots can include anything  from mech suits to cyborgs  and the spare parts in between change  your batteries and bring yourself back  online because these are the best robot  movies  of all time set in the 29th century  wally finds a world that's been  devastated by human carelessness  and global warming as a result people  now live on distant spaceships  waiting for the earth to heal the humans  on these massive star liners continue to  be lazy and destructive  relying on machines to carry them around  wally is one of the last cleaning robots  left on earth  he has a simple and joyful life  collecting random objects and drifting  through the desolation  until he meets eve a robot sent to  identify  signs of life  [Music]  [Applause]  wary and eve's relationship is tender  and sweet they fall in love and  eventually find evidence that humans can  finally return to rebuild earth  amazingly many of the robots in wall-e  including eve  display far more empathy compassion and  humanity than most of the humans in the  film james cameron's a terminator was a  groundbreaking robot movie when it came  out in 1984  but his own sequel in 1991 blew the  original out of the water  terminator 2 judgement day featured both  the revamped version of the original  robot played by  arnold schwarzenegger and the t-1000 who  remains one of the most amazing robot  creations  ever put to screen this shape-shifting  robot played by robert patrick has a  base form of liquid metal which is  thrilling to watch in action  the practical and digital effects in  terminator 2 judgement day  are even better now thanks to hd tvs and  the battle between the two robots are  just as epic  it's rare when a sequel surpasses the  original but terminator 2 easily  outperforms the first film ridley  scott's 1979 sci-fi horror film alien  introduced audiences to extraterrestrial  beasts with acid for blood and creepy  face-hugging creatures that impregnate  humans through their mouths  but alien also featured the horrifying  revelation that ash the chief science  officer aboard the nostromo  is actually a robot and worse he's been  given the order to bring back the  xenomorph creature intact  and the crew is totally expendable when  our hero ripley finds out about ash the  robot tries to attack her  but suffers an android meltdown and  loses his head  ash represents the worst of robot nature  where his core code forces him into  terrible acts of violence  in alex garland's disturbing ex machina  we meet caleb  a programmer who has won a vacation to  the remote estate of nathan bateman  his company's ceo more importantly he's  won the unique opportunity to see what  new projects nathan is developing  before anyone else does nathan  introduces caleb to a robot he designed  named ava  hoping she shows signs of consciousness  through their interactions  although ava resembles a machine in  every way other than her face  feet and hands her personality is so  charming that caleb finds himself  falling in love  as caleb loses trust in the brash and  erratic nathan  we learn that ava has plans of her own  plans that exclude both men  the special effects in ex machina are  spectacular and the performances are  remarkable  even though the plot focuses on common  artificial intelligence themes  ex machina is a compelling addition to  the ai canon  hoverhoven's dystopian 1987 action  thriller robocop  is set in a future detroit on the verge  of total collapse  after a shootout leaves officer alex  murphy dead his body is taken into a  pilot program  designed to play cyborg officers in  dangerous parts of the city  the longer alex's robocop however the  more he is haunted by memories of his  former life  and his brutal demise when robocop  realizes that his own boss was  responsible for alex's fall  he goes on a wild rampage for justice in  the film we see the tension between his  human soul and his robot body  by the end our hero must find new ways  to integrate both halves of himself  ultimately the film suggests that human  and machine can co-exist in one body  based on a novel by philip k dick ridley  scott's 1982 cyberpunk masterpiece blade  runner  is a narrative feast featuring sweeping  scenes of an imaginary 2019 the film  introduces us to a group of human-like  robots  known as replicants these robots are  essentially slaves that were designed to  work for humans  what's even worse is that they only live  for four years with such a short shelf  life a group of replicants decides to do  something about it  harrison ford plays decker a human cop  who sets out to destroy the escaped  replicants  along the way he begins to see how human  these beings really are  and depending on which version of blade  runner you've seen his own reality comes  into question  the robots in blade runner are  indistinguishable from humans  unlike many other robot stories where  the inhumanity and physical differences  are highlighted  plus the moving tears in rain speech at  the film's end elevates blade runner to  one of the greatest films of all time  thomas anderson is a low-level  information tech clerk who enjoys  occasionally going down the rabbit hole  as a hacker called neo  when a radical named trinity informs him  that the infamous morpheus can tell him  everything he wants to know about the  matrix  neo jumps at the opportunity but not  before the evil agent smith attempts to  silence neo  and keep him from his destiny the matrix  features some of the more monstrous  robots in sci-fi history  these beings appear as jellyfish-like  creatures with many eyes and tentacles  which is about as far from human as a  robot can look they harvest humans as a  renewable energy source and to keep them  from fighting back  the robots created an elaborate computer  program that convinces people they're  actually in the real world  with its high concept and unique  portrayal of robotic beasts the matrix  stands out as one of the best  robot movies steven spielberg's robot  opus ai artificial intelligence is set  in the 22nd century  where a devastated world is marked by  extreme economic inequality  robots known as mecca were created to  serve all functions  and even show up as surrogate children  for those who can't have kids of their  own  david is one such child but gifted to  monica swinton  after her terminally ill son was forced  into hibernation until a cure is  available  david knows he's a robot but once he  imprints on moniker as her son  he becomes completely attached to his  new mom after monica's real son wakes  from his slumber and returns home  david is flung into the wild world  outside the swinton home  a world where mecca are hunted tortured  and destroyed in a beautiful narrative  that borrows from pinocchio david  searches for the blue fairy so he can  become a real boy  ai is a heartbreaking commentary on what  it means to be human  as told through the eyes of a robot  child horror master guillermo del toro  took a huge leap from his usual affair  with the epic robot battle extravaganza  pacific rim  in the film a deep underwater rift opens  up on earth releasing a set of monsters  known as the kaiju who terrorized the  planet  in retaliation humans create equally  monstrous robots manned by pilots  sent to combat the growing kaiju threat  where pacific rim differs from the other  mecca movies  is that the robots are controlled by  humans as opposed to having their own  consciousness  the robots in pacific rim are simply  human weapons the real  tension arises from pilots rawley  beckett and marco mori  face their own dramatic histories to  properly overcome the kaiju threat  the special effects are wild and the  action never stops  with a story driven by emotional  conflict pacific rim  is easily one of the best robot movies  of all time  based on ireland's novel of the same  name the stepford wives remains one of  the most chilling robot movies of all  time  the movie follows would-be manhattan  photographer joanna eberhardt and her  husband walter  after they moved to a small connecticut  town called stepford  joanna feels stifled by the community  even though it's beautiful  she finds the other women in town  horribly boring and is deeply disturbed  by the local men's association  headed by its creepy president dale  cobra thankfully joanna meets bobby a  vocal feminist who would also love to  dismantle the strange patriarchy  surrounding them  that is until one day bobby starts  acting just like all the other stepford  wives  from there joanna discovers that the men  in town have been replacing the women  with robots  offering commentary on gender marriage  and social control  considering its 1975 release this film  has aged remarkably well  batteries not included is a unique robot  movie that features an elderly couple at  its center  when a greedy manhattan property  developer named lacey tries to take over  a rent-controlled apartment building  managed by frank and faye riley  the rileys and their tenants resist for  as long as they can  one night after lacy's goons damage the  building a flying robot creature known  as a fix-it appears the fixes repair all  the damage  as well as other structural problems in  the building in a fascinating term for a  robot movie  mama and papa fix it actually have a set  of babies and by the end of the film  there's a rather large community of  fixit robots residing in new york  set in 2020 where robot fighting has  replaced boxing  charlie kenton is a former prize fighter  whose pivot to robot boxing has been  rocky  with his brash personality charlie finds  himself deeper in debt and without a  robot to bet on  well that is until he finds out his  ex-girlfriend's past and his son max is  now involved in a custody dispute  between his aunt deborah and her wealthy  husband  marvin seeing an opportunity charlie  extorts marvin for 50 000  so he can buy a classic boxing robot he  also gets stuck with max for the summer  he was cut from much of the same cloth  as his estranged father  max is into robot boxing as well and  turns out to be a huge help to charlie  especially after discovering a junkyard  robot named atom  the movie features incredible fight  scenes with an army of actual boxing  robots created using the same technology  that brought jurassic park and avatar to  life there are also absolutely charming  moments where max and atom dance  together real steel is not only one of  the best robot movies of all time  but it also comes wrapped in a  heartwarming story about the intense  bonds between a father  and his son set in 1957 during the  height of american tensions with russia  the iron giant starts with a mysterious  object crashing into the water  near the small and quaint town of  rockwell maine the next day a young  local named hogarth  discovers that the object is in fact an  enormous extraterrestrial robot who is  both friendly and curious about the  planet upon which he landed  due to the political tensions of the  cold war era a xenophobic us agent  is convinced that something far more  sinister is taking place in rockwell  than a robot who's ended up on the wrong  planet  over the course of the film hogarth and  the giant's friendship grow stronger  but their relationship is eventually  challenged by the american government  the giant has an opportunity to prove he  was never a threat to humans  and that people are in fact their own  worst enemies with lush colours and a  powerful story that ends on a hopeful  note the iron giant is one of the most  beautiful robot tales ever told  fritz lang's 1927 masterpiece metropolis  has long been celebrated by film  scholars and fans alike  its story was far ahead of its time and  featured a female robot  who's made to look like a human  anti-capitalist organizer  in a plot by the ruling class who then  ruined her reputation to maintain the  status quo  it's complicated yes metropolis might  require more suspension of disbelief  than other robot films on this list  but the fact that this movie was made in  1927 is pretty impressive  plus it not only features technology  that simply didn't exist at the time but  it also has a very obvious  anti-capitalist message  that remains wildly relevant today check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  you
 

